      "title": "The Accidental Discovery of Penicillin",
      "source": "예시 글",
      "paragraphs": [
        "In 1928, the Scottish scientist Alexander Fleming returned from a holiday and found mold growing on one of his lab dishes. Around the mold, the bacteria had died. Instead of throwing the dish away, Fleming began to {{investigate|investigate}}.",
        "The mold produced a substance he named penicillin. It took more than ten years for other researchers to {{develop|develop}} a way to make it in large amounts. Fleming's story is often used to show that a good scientist does not {{ignore|ignore}} a surprising result."
